diff --git a/doc/source/index.rst b/doc/source/index.rst
index 2d1e9f8..cff62a1 100644
--- a/doc/source/index.rst
+++ b/doc/source/index.rst
@@ -653,6 +653,21 @@ With async code you can use AsyncRetrying.
       except RetryError:
           pass
 
+Inside an ``async for`` loop, the attempt is also an async context manager, so
+``async with attempt:`` behaves exactly like ``with attempt:``.
+
+.. testcode::
+
+   from tenacity import AsyncRetrying, RetryError, stop_after_attempt
+
+   async def function():
+      try:
+          async for attempt in AsyncRetrying(stop=stop_after_attempt(3)):
+              async with attempt:
+                  raise Exception('My code is failing!')
+      except RetryError:
+          pass
+
 In both cases, you may want to set the result to the attempt so it's available
 in retry strategies like ``retry_if_result``. This can be done accessing the
 ``retry_state`` property:
